WEBVTT

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:07.170
It's once again time to think of a super move
that's good for a Shadow Mistress like me!

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.670
And so, this is my third time making this pose!

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:15.670
Previously, I asked Lico and the boss for help.
I wonder who will give me some attack ideas this time?

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.250
<b>SUPER MOVE</b>

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.250
<b>ANRI SATA'S</b>

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.750
Don't worry about tomorrow,
for tomorrow will take care of itself!

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.130
I just thought that up!

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.790
A super move? You need to build stamina
before doing anything else, Shamiko.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.750
<b>OMOIZAWA WEINERS</b>

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.750
<b>WE DELIVER EVERYWHERE</b>

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.750
<b>AND ANYWHERE</b>

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.710
Besides, why would you come and ask me?
I'm in the middle of helping run the family biz!

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.750
You wanna get tougher? Then eat some meat!

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.040
Run farther? Eat meat! Punch stronger? Eat meat!

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.830
Y-you make a good point. I'll take 200 grams.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.380
Just 200? Or 300?

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.130
M-make it 300 grams.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.040
Shiny shine!

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:55.210
<b>Heh heh...</b>

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:55.210
<b>Heh heh...</b>

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:47.130
Don't you want to get stronger?
Then you'll need more than that!

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:55.130
Heh, heh, heh, heh...

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.130
O-okay, 400 grams.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.210
<b>DOUBLE MEAT WHAMMY SPECIAL</b>

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.790
This is Anri's super move.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.130
She calls it the: "Double Meat Whammy Special."

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:58.670
<b>Heh heh...</b>

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.790
Heh, heh, heh, heh...

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.580
Shimmer, glimmer!

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:02.130
<b>SION OGURA'S SUPER MOVE</b>

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.080
Chance only favors the mind which is prepared!

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.250
How are things going? You want a super move?

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.880
One of those surefire winning attacks, right?

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.920
I'm so happy that you came
just to ask for my advice, Shamiko!

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.290
Okay. Let me explain my super move.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.290
It's called: Organic Synthesis!

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.920
<b>ORGANIC SYNTHESIS</b>

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.920
Wow, that sounds like a legit super move!

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.080
First, you have to privately import
blabbidyblah from yaddayadda.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:34.290
<b>First, you have to privately</b>

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:34.290
<b>import ****** from ****...</b>

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:34.290
<b>Borrow a ********* and a ****</b>

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:34.290
<b>from the science lab</b>

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:34.290
<b>and use the vapors to *******.</b>

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.960
Then, you slowly mix it together
with ********* that's of a high purity.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:26.580
Then, you slowly mix it together
with adeebladeeploo that's of a high purity.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:34.290
<b>When that happens, dehydrate</b>

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:30.500
Borrow a shamafuzehoraba and a wobblyblop
from the science lab and use the vapor to noodbood.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:34.290
<b>using the ************* and...</b>

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.380
When that happens, dehydrate
using the toyalodaronjo and...

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.380
X950podranbelopopopopepepewoodle is complete!

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:35.420
<b>IS COMPLETE!!</b>

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.330
See? Look at how smooth and white it is!

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:40.960
Let's leave and pretend this never happened.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:43.210
Sounds good. We're having chicken steaks tonight!

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.880
Check out that summer sun, yo!

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.170
Mikan! Don't you have any homework to do?

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.380
I'm transferring to your school this September
and as luck would have it

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.500
<b>Waaah...</b>

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.500
<b>It never ends...</b>

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.460
the homework from my old school doesn't carry over!

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.500
<b>YIPPEE</b>

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.710
Which means I'm free to do
whatever I want over summer vacation!

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.500
That's the privilege of being a transfer student!

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.500
Yippee!

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.960
I'm so jealous!
Ohohoho~ Ohohoho~ Ohohoho~<b></b>

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.460
<b>Ohohohohoho</b>

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.460
<b>Ohohohohoho</b>

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:03.460
<b>Ohohohohoho</b>

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.420
I just can't stop my smug laughter!
Ohohoho~ Ohohoho~ Ohohoho~<b></b>

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:10.750
<b>TRANSFER INTERVIEW</b>

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.290
And so, to make sure that doesn't happen, I've prepared
some homework and short essays for you to do.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.880
Also, this is all the material
that will be on the post-vacation test.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:10.630
Oh no.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.500
<b>AROUND HERE</b>

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.750
I'm originally from around these parts.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.000
<b>AROUND HERE</b>

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.960
Wow!

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:32.080
The excitement has just begun!

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:39.670
I have a feeling that a miracle will occur

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:46.920
A novice's skill is enough. Now, let's go!

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:49.880
It's all or nothing. We can go anywhere

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:54.630
Let me hear more even the sound of the core

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:59.420
If you and I put our hands together, there is nothing to fear

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.920
When I'm at a loss what to do,

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:08.080
I'll remember that you are here for me

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.580
You and I look up at the same sky

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:19.960
We smile at each other and overcome hardship, too

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:25.210
Doing our best for someone

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.790
Isn't bad, too,

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:32.380
We are side by side again today

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.630
The excitement has just begun

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:52.040
<b>THE ANCESTOR'S DOJO?!</b>

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:52.040
<b>DEMONKIND'S ULTIMATE WEAPON!</b>

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.750
Mikan!

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.130
I've gotten pretty used to living on my own.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:59.630
Except for lately, all of my trash
has been piling up into a indecent mess.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:02.880
It's always hard to learn
the local trash rules after moving.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.000
I need to figure out when and where to dump it.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.630
<b>Animalia, Arthropoda, Insecta,</b>

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:11.630
<b>Blattodea: Smokybrown cockroa-</b>

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:10.750
Animalia, Arthropoda, Insecta,

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.420
Blattodea: Smokybrown cockroa-

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.170
All the birds just went flying off.
And a dog is barking in the distance.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:22.250
Meanwhile, I'm cleaning up in front of our apartment!

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:23.960
Shamikoooooo!

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.710
Good morning, Mikan.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:28.750
Yes, hello! Oh, it's awful, one finally showed up!

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:33.130
You know! One of them!
The black, glossy, and speedy things!

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.630
Ah, you mean a cockroach?

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:36.710
Are you crazy?! Don't just blurt it out like that!

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.330
Call them by a cuter nickname,
like "Groachy" or something!

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.710
Wait, does that mean insects don't bother you?

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.580
There are a lot of little openings in our house,
so I'm used to tiny creatures sneaking in.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:50.000
Cockroaches don't scare me since they have
no attack power. Momo's way scarier than they are!

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.580
Sometimes what you consider "okay"
is totally out of whack...

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.040
Here. Use these.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.130
<b>Scorseies</b>

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.330
What are these for?

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:58.580
Huh? They're tissues for you to scoop up
the cockroach and release it outside.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.460
Scoop it up?! That's a foreign concept to me!

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.880
But cockroaches don't bite or anything.

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:06.000
It's horseflies, wasps, and longhorned beetles
that you really have to watch out for.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:10.670
Longhorned beetles in particular have a way stronger
bite than you would think given their size.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.170
It hurts about 50 times more than you imagine.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.830
So, if you think about it,
cockroaches are kinder than other insects.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.710
That's not the problem here!

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:18.750
Right, of course...

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.790
Meanwhile, completely unbeknownst to everyone,

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:27.500
Mikan's distress was causing Momo
to suffer the modest effects of her curse.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:30.330
Listen, I just can't handle those little black buggers.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.420
They freak me out,
so will you come help clean up my room?

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:36.040
Roger that! If we spot any cockroaches,
then I'll scoop them up right away!

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:34.330
<b>ZOOP</b>

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:38.380
<b>Scorseies</b>

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.380
No scooping! Just forget about the scooping!

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:42.210
"Groachys" are pretty fifthly, you know.
It's best not to touch them.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:43.960
If one shows up, you gotta take 'em out.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.330
You're going to kill it?

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:49.210
It did nothing wrong.
All it did was exist and it gets attacked.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:51.330
I feel awful, since it reminds me of demons...

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.080
Oh jeez! Fine then!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:55.250
We'll think of a way to let it escape
without scooping it up!

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.540
The Groachy that I saw earlier is still hiding out.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:02.790
Be careful. It ran somewhere in all of the garbage.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.080
You know, the damage to my door still hasn't been fixed.

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:10.880
I'm sorry about that. We broke your door
and gave you such a hard time first thing in the morning.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.330
That's okay.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:15.580
It was an emergency, right?

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:18.920
Forget about saying sorry.
I would rather hear a "thank you" instead.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:22.170
And in return, I hope that you'll save me
whenever I get into trouble.

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:23.630
Sure thing!

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.130
For starters, I'll save you from the Groachy.

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.170
<b>Scorseies</b>

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:26.170
<b>ZOOP...</b>

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:26.130
I said no scooping!

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:28.130
<b>Garblaaaaaaage</b>

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:28.130
Garblaaaaaaage.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.920
We can probably find the Groachy that ran away
if we clean things up little by little.

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.040
Sounds like a plan.

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:35.130
<b>TIMID</b>

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.210
I'm sorry that my place is such an awful mess.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.540
Let's start by sorting the garbage over here first.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.580
<b>MIKAN CAN              MIKAN CAN             MIKAN CAN              MIKAN</b>

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.580
Mikan can, mikan can, mikan, can, mikan.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:49.290
<b>MIKAN CAN  MIKAN CAN  MIKAN</b>

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:45.750
Mikan can, mikan can, mikan, can, mikan.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.080
Mikan can, mikan, mikan, can, mikan can.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:51.380
You don't have to check through everything one by one!

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.750
<b>Glare</b>

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:51.920
Tee-hee.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.080
<b>PLONK</b>

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.080
I still haven't figured out the sorting rules.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:58.880
Oh, right. I nearly forgot that Mikan came here
all by herself at Momo's request.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:00.210
Just for my sake.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:03.830
I'm sorry. You have to adapt
to this new lifestyle all because of me.

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:05.960
Don't look so glum.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.630
Besides, I've always wanted to try living on my own!

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.040
It's a good learning experience!

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:11.710
So don't sweat it, Shamiko.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:16.920
The best method to stop someone
from going over to the dark side

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:18.830
is to hit them with a healthy dose
of the power of friendship!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.170
M-Mikan?

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:21.880
Shamiko, you need to back away from Momo.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.040
Sorry, Mikan. I know that wasn't easy for you.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.460
Don't mention it!

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.330
Be grateful you have the powerful friendship
of someone as awesome as me!

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:31.880
<b>DOOM              DOOM                     DOOM                  DOOM                  DOOM</b>

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:31.880
<b>DOOM</b>

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:31.880
<b>DOOM</b>

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:35.250
Fwashoooooooooooooooooooooooooom!

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:39.670
Hey, Mikan? There's one more thing
I'm a little concerned about...

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:40.500
Huh?

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.080
I feel like you get burdened
with too many outrageous requests.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.500
Oh, is that all that's bothering you?

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:50.790
It's totally fine. Momo and I are far
from being strangers, you know.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.830
But I have to admit, I've never seen her
be so dark and grim before.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:57.880
It's been 10 years since we first met. We've both
taken on outrageous requests from each other.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.130
10 years...

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.330
GLEAAAM!

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.830
<b>GLEAAAM!</b>

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.290
Do I detect envy? Are you feeling jealous?

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.960
Ugh! N-no, I am most certainly not!
She's my arch-enemy, dang it!

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.210
<b>Non-burnable Garbage</b>

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.210
<b>Wed</b>

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.210
<b>Can, Glass, Plastic Bottles</b>

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.210
<b>Tue & Fri</b>

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.210
<b>Burnable Garbage</b>

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.210
<b>Mon & Thurs</b>

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:08.210
But thinking about it...

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.750
Only about 3 months have passed
since I first met Momo.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:17.330
I imagine she has a lot of her own stories
from before we met that I'm not even aware of.

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:20.290
And those experiences are not something
I can fully share in.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:23.460
It makes me feel... frustrated.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.920
Wait, couldn't I sneak a peak at them?

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.830
My succubus powers would make it easy.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:30.580
No, no, no, no! Forget it, forget it, forget it!

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:32.250
Heave-hoooooo!

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:33.250
I've never seen anyone throw out the trash so intensely...

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:34.710
I'm getting rid of the garbage in my heart!

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.920
Go, go, go, go! Take this!

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:37.830
And that!

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:41.170
Stop it, boy. That isn't a toy to play with.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:44.040
I'm so sorry about him, ladies.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:45.540
Oh, no worries.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:49.960
Well, that certainly helped to make my place
feel more spacious. But there's still some trash left.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:54.710
<b>HUGE SALE</b>

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:54.710
<b>EARN 5 TIMES</b>

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:54.710
<b>THE POINTS!</b>

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.460
Oh! Do you mind if I take those old fliers?

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:54.540
Fine by me. What are you going to use them for?

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.210
To make tiny garbage cans!

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.540
Tiny what now?

00:08:57.790 --> 00:08:59.540
My mom taught me how to make them!

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.130
She uses them while cooking to collect
kitchen scraps and chuck them all in one go!

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:03.040
They're really convenient!

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.630
Oh wow! That means I could eat mikans,
dekopons, and iyokans together

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:08.790
without having to throw away the scraps every time!

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:09.540
How ingenious!

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:11.000
I know, right? It's amazing!

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.540
My mom is a real wizard at making stuff out of old fliers!

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:15.040
It's a phoenix!

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:17.000
<b>PHOENIX</b>

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.000
Holy poultry!

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:18.710
A phoenix?

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:21.130
That one is really difficult to pull off.

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:24.670
So I recommend you try making
a shuriken or paper popper!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:25.790
<b>SCHWING!</b>

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.960
Sorry, but I don't get what those could be useful for...

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.000
<b>SCHWING!</b>

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.920
Ah! There it is, Mikan! The Groachy!

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:31.710
Wha-?!

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:32.920
Bwalgh.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.710
Let's hurry and scoop it right out of here!

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.710
<b>Scorseies</b>

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.710
<b>ZOOP</b>

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:37.170
<b>WOOSH!!</b>

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:37.170
Dag gummit! We ain't scooping
nothin with yer consarned tissues!

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.170
Wah! It went back into hiding!

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:39.880
Yeek!

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:43.380
Shamiko! Can't you enter the Groachy's dream
and hypnotize it into freezing up or something?!

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:48.130
<b>Scorseies</b>

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.420
Well, that would require going into deep sleep.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.330
Then lay your butt down and get to snoozing right now!

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:48.040
Hey...

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:53.170
Mikan's curse has been activating
and tormenting me the entire morning...

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.000
Momo!

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:57.710
First my water pipe burst and
then I fell through a hole that opened in the ditch...

00:09:57.710 --> 00:10:01.750
Plus, Shamiko totally forgot to steam my rice
for breakfast. I knew something was wrong.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:04.330
Hold up, you make Shamiko steam your rice?

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:08.250
Don't ask questions because if you press me on that
I'm gonna slip to the dark side again.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.250
This meeting is adjourned.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.290
<b>THIS MEETING</b>

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:10.290
<b>IS ADJOURNED</b>

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.290
Huh?! That's not fair! You're such a weasel!

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.210
Unfair! Unfair!

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:11.170
<b>SMACK!</b>

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:12.250
<b>SMACK!</b>

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:19.210
Unfair! Unfair! Unfair! Unfair!

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:12.880
Bugs, huh?

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.250
<b>Unfair! Unfair!</b>

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.250
<b>SMACK!</b>

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.630
I've had a tough time dealing with those myself, lately.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:14.250
<b>Unfair! Unfair!</b>

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:14.250
<b>SMACK!</b>

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:15.750
<b>Unfair! Unfair!</b>

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:15.750
<b>SMACK!</b>

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.710
You aren't comfortable with bugs either, Momo?

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:16.750
<b>Unfair! Unfair!</b>

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:16.750
<b>SMACK!</b>

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:19.210
Any type that crawls around on its legs...

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:18.750
<b>Unfair! Unfair!</b>

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:18.750
<b>SMACK!</b>

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:20.880
<b>SCRATCH</b>

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:20.880
<b>SCRATCH</b>

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:20.880
<b>SCRATCH</b>

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:29.670
<b>SCRATCH</b>

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:29.670
<b>SCRATCH</b>

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:29.670
<b>SCRATCH</b>

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:29.670
Scratch, scratch, scratch, scratch

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:24.040
For some reason, seeing bugs that have legs
really unsettles me as of late...

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:26.670
It puts me on the verge of a Fresh Peach Heart Shower.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.670
So you haven't fully recovered from that trauma...

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:31.630
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:34.670
Since we live in an apartment designed
to exude an "abandoned ruins" vibe,

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:35.790
then it's inevitable that bugs will come in.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.580
Ruins?

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.500
We're gonna have to do something to change that.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:40.380
Let's make a bug warding barrier.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:43.830
It'll be just like the magical girl warding barrier
that's hanging on your front door, Shamiko.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.130
Except much simpler.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.130
<b>RUINS?</b>

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:46.130
Ruins?

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:50.710
Crafting an intricate barrier that's super strong
would require time and expertise we don't have.

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.080
But my sister did teach me how to make a basic one.

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.580
Do you have any old fliers lying around, Mikan?

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.290
I did, but we used them all to make tiny boxes!

00:10:58.670 --> 00:10:59.670
Huh? Why do that?

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:03.000
So that I can eat a bunch of mikans, dekopons,
iyokans, pondarins, and banpeiyus

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:06.580
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:11:00.830 --> 00:11:06.580
<b>DEKOPON</b>

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:06.580
<b>IYOKAN</b>

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:06.580
<b>PONDARIN</b>

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:06.580
<b>BANPEIYU</b>

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.460
without having to get up to
throw away the scraps every time.

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:08.830
It looks like you're making a technical drawing.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:12.040
Yep. Creating magic circles is a lot like drafting.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:14.630
You have to sketch them out
in accordance to a set of rules.

00:11:14.670 --> 00:11:16.460
Hey, Shamiko. Do an eraser run on this for me.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:17.580
What's an "eraser run"?

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.000
It's when you run an eraser over the entire drawing.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.170
I see.

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:24.380
Whenever my sister made a barrier like this,
I would do eraser runs or paint daubs to help out.

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:25.710
What's a "paint daub"?!

00:11:25.710 --> 00:11:28.210
<b>3 HOURS LATER</b>

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.630
Here, guys. I brought coffee!

00:11:30.630 --> 00:11:32.790
If you hold it up to the light,
you can make out any skewing from behind.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:35.670
Hey, is it just me or have
you forgotten about the Groachy?

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:36.830
So, is it ready now?

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:37.960
Still needs the finishing touch.

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.960
Shamiko, infuse this magic circle that I drew
with some of your magic.

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:42.130
Huh? You want me to?!

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:46.080
All you have to do is touch it with your weapon
while invoking a wish or prayer in your head.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:47.290
Okay then...

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:49.250
MAGIC GOOOOO!

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:49.540
<b>SLAM</b>

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:51.130
It lit up!

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.330
You activated it. The barrier's ready now.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:57.250
<b>HINATSUKI</b>

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:57.460
Just keep this posted on the front door
and bugs shouldn't bother you for a while.

00:11:57.540 --> 00:11:59.960
That's a huge relief! Thank you, guys!

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:07.380
By the way, I noticed you said "a while."
Does that mean the barrier will wear off eventually?

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:10.670
How long it stays active is proportional
to the quality of magic its infused with.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.210
The quality of... the magic...?

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.210
<b>HINATSUKI</b>

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:16.210
<b>WOMP...</b>

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:19.830
Eek! It showed up again!

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.830
Didn't even last half a day, huh?

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.380
My magic needs work.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:28.460
Hiyah! Hooyah! Booyah! Fooyah! Hoooooyah!

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:27.080
Here, keep it going. Next, next, next.

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:29.080
Great, only 10 more barriers to go!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:30.170
Is this an endless marathon or what?!

00:12:30.170 --> 00:12:31.710
The strange fatigue I'm feeling is staggering!

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:33.330
Hey! Why am I the only one doing this?!

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:35.330
Get off your lazy butts and help me!

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.460
I'd love to give you a hand, but...

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.670
You're learning how to better emit your magic
every time you do it.

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:42.540
So this is great training for you, Shamiko.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:51.580
Once you improve the quality of your magic,
one of these babies can last a whole month!

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.290
I... can't stay awake...

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.250
I made us some mikan tea.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:13:00.790
Don't give up, Shamiko! Surpass the pressure of crunch
time and become a demon girl of the highest caliber!

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:04.000
It smells wonderful. This will help me get a good rest.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.330
No sleeping. Just a little more to go!

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:32.920
<b>GOOD DAY TO DRY THE FUTONS DANCE</b>

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.250
Slide.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.380
Spin.

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:23.500
Spin, spin.

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.670
Spin, spin, spin, and then...

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.460
La, la, la~!

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.790
A pleasantly warm day with a nice, refreshing breeze!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:37.380
Yuko, dear. It's time for you to use the power
of the rod that your father bequeathed to you!

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:38.460
Roger that!

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:42.750
Whachamacallit Rod! Laundry-drying pole mooooode!

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:46.750
We're selling poles. Get your bamboo poles here.

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:46.080
<b>WE'RE SELLING POLES</b>

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.080
<b>GET YOUR BAMBOO POLES HERE</b>

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.630
Two for 1,000 yen.

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:52.880
Life has become truly wonderful now that we can hang
all 3 of our futons out to dry together.

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:54.380
I'm glad I was born a demon!

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.580
Demons who get to sleep on super soft futons!

00:13:57.080 --> 00:14:02.500
That's the price from 30 years ago.
I've been saying this over and over for 30 years now.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:06.210
Hey Momo! The Whachamacallit Rod
is proving really handy!

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:07.880
Shamiko?

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:08.580
Heh-heh!

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:08.630
<b>HEH-HEH!</b>

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:11.210
Give me your blanket so we can dry that out, too.

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:14.420
You seriously need to think
of better ways to use that rod.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:16.830
<b>Float                  Float</b>

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:20.790
You have a nice scent, Momo.
It's like I'm smelling fresh peaches.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:26.880
Sniff, sniff. Sniff, sniff. Sniff, sniff.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:25.250
That's just how you're perceiving the waves
coming from my ether body, but forget that!

00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:26.880
It doesn't matter what I smell like!

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:30.210
That rod is an important object
meant to protect you, Shamiko.

00:14:30.210 --> 00:14:32.330
You need to come up with a more practical use for it.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:33.540
Practical use?

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:38.040
<b>MOMO</b>

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:38.040
<b>YOU ROCK!</b>

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:38.040
<b>COME TO THE DARK SIDE</b>

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:42.460
<b>MOMO</b>

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:42.460
<b>YOU ROCK!</b>

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:42.460
<b>COME TO THE DARK SIDE</b>

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:39.500
What the heck is that?

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:40.750
An idol fan.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:42.210
You change that back right now.

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:43.750
Shoop, shoop, shoop.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:45.790
Also, that fan is not even remotely stick-shaped!

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.500
But it seems kinda stick-like to me!

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.540
Your neural pathways must be super wonky, I swear!

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:52.420
<b>FANS ARE KINDA STICK-LIKE</b>

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:52.420
<b>HMPH</b>

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:52.420
<b>HMPH</b>

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:52.210
I think it's just fine classified as a stick.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:56.210
You don't have long to wait until I get screentime!

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.080
I'm going to help out my Big Sis, too!

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:04.170
Look, all I'm saying is that it doesn't make sense,
your rod can only transform into "stick-shaped" stuff.

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:06.290
Because it's been doing way more than that!

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:12.170
"Stick: A long and slender piece of wood, metal,
or bamboo that could fit in a person's hand."

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:14.460
Wait, so this doesn't technically count as a stick?!

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.250
Huh? It just reverted back to normal!

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:20.040
Ah! So it doesn't work if you start questioning yourself.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:23.500
Aw, crap. That means it would have
been better to let you stay dumb.

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:24.790
Hey, what'd you say?!

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:27.290
As I recall, when you were in the dreamscape,

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:29.420
you turned it into some kind of
"Overpowered Weapon" that defeated everything.

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:32.420
O-overpowered weapoooooooooon!

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:35.210
T-too heavy...

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:46.170
That means you can make things that don't exist, right?
Like fictional weapons and such.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.830
I... I wanna see that!

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:51.710
Yitian Jian! Gungnir! Amenonuhoko!

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.830
Huh? What are those?

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:57.750
The Yitian Jian is a famous sword from Chinese
mythology said to slice through rocks like butter!

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:57.750
Slice, slice!

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:02.040
Gungnir is a spear from Norse mythology that
always hits and even comes back when you throw it!

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.040
I strike! And then come back!

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:03.790
Oh, cool...

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:12.500
<b>AMENONUHOKO                                                                  SPEAR FROM JAPANESE MYTHOLOGY</b>

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:12.500
<b>There were two gods, Izanagi and Izanami,</b>

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:12.500
<b>who used this spear to somehow churn the chaotic world,</b>

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:12.500
<b>After that, they kinda did a bunch of other stuff</b>

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:12.500
<b>and created the islands of Japan.</b>

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:05.750
Amenonuhoko is a mythological spear

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.960
that can be used to create stuff by churning chaos!

00:16:08.040 --> 00:16:10.170
What do you mean by "churning chaos"?! I'm not sure

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:12.500
I'll be meeting any chaos during the course of my life!

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:14.170
Something that doesn't exist, huh?

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:18.290
Shamiko, I wanna run a test by having you
make a pole that's 30 kilometers long.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:19.500
30 kilometers?!

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.170
I wanna know if it can break the stratosphere or not.

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:24.880
If it seems like it might fall over, then I'll handle it.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.580
We're really gonna do this?

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:27.710
Let's head outside.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.580
H-here we go!

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:33.790
A 30 kilometer long pooooole!

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:37.500
Nope... it's not working.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:39.000
Hey, Momo?

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:42.330
Okay. Then make a pair of chopsticks
made from pure gold.

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:43.580
B-but why?!

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:45.420
I wanna sell one of them off and then find out

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:46.880
what happens when you undo the transformation.

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.460
Momo, please. I'm upside down.

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:47.210
<b>Momo</b>

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:50.630
<b>POP</b>

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:52.460
Nope, it didn't work!

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.670
But I can make regular wooden chopsticks!

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:56.500
I guess you can only cheat
when you're in the dreamscape.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.040
How do you even come up with these crazy ideas?!

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:05.750
<b>Momo</b>

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:03.040
I think it's more likely that Shamiko
is subconsciously restraining herself.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.670
She doesn't have enough magic power
to bring the impossible into reality.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.580
Your dominion is the dreamscape.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.290
Why don't you try training inside of my sealed space?

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:14.130
Practice using your imagination inside the dreamscape
and gradually apply that experience to the real world,

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:16.710
then you might have more luck
with transforming complex things!

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:17.880
G-great idea!

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:19.080
Hee-hee-hee-hee...

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:19.210
<b>Hee-hee</b>

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:19.210
<b>Hee-hee</b>

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:21.710
I'm totally onboard with the golden chopsticks plan.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:23.420
Too bad! I'm not going to do that!

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:31.630
<b>PLEASE BE SURE TO HOLD ME UPRIGHT</b>

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:27.210
Being upside down for too long sucks
because it makes me dizzy.

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.290
Oh? I thought I was holding you right side up.

00:17:29.500 --> 00:17:31.540
Hold on, Momo. Are you doing this on purpose?

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:34.380
Alright, I'm off to train my imagination in the dreamscape!

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.000
Do you want to tag along, Ryo?

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:37.790
Is that possible?

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:40.210
I should be able to summon
any of Shamiko's blood relatives.

00:17:40.750 --> 00:17:45.000
I'll go! I wanna see my Big Sis wield a legendary weapon
in battle against tens of thousands of enemies!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:45.960
It'll be awesome!

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:47.790
Don't raise the bar so high, please!

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.710
What about me, Ms. Lilith?

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:52.420
You're not one of our relatives, so I can't summon you.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:55.290
Vessel tickets.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:18:00.460
<b>FREE VESSEL</b>

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:58.790
You know I want those so bad that I could spawn
arms from my statue, but it's just not possible!

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:00.330
Go take a dip on the dark side and then ask me!

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:02.210
Heh-heh-heh-heh...

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:03.000
Ta-da!

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:05.420
<b>IT'S BEEN A WHILE</b>

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:05.420
<b>SO WORSHIP</b>

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:05.420
<b>MY GLORIOUS RETURN!</b>

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.330
A pleasure to have you, my cute descendants!

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:06.380
She's blonde!

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:09.290
This is the first time you've seen me
in my true form, huh, Ryoko?

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:11.210
You must be stunned by how grand and majestic I am.

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:13.290
Don't be shy, go on and revere my glorious form!

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:15.210
It's like my sister unlocked an alternate color.

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:17.250
Whaddya mean "alternate color"?

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:20.000
"Alternate color" is a term used in fighting games

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.420
and more for whenever multiple players
select the same character

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:25.080
and a palette swap is used
to differentiate one from the other.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.000
You suddenly turned into a motormouth, Shamiko.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:30.630
But in our case, I was born after you were, so technically
yours is the original color and I'm the alternate.

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:32.210
You just can't help yourself, huh?

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.080
Sorry, I'm a big fan of video games.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.710
Fair enough. Now prepare your rod
and let's get down to business!

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:39.500
This is the dreamscape where
the mighty succubi slumber!

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.000
And I've got the perfect target for you to practice on.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:44.130
The extreme sparring brigade of cute Lilith sandbags!

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:45.420
Come on!

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:45.420
<b>RUMBLE           RUMBLE                                     RUMBLE             RUMBLE</b>

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:50.790
This army is the manifestation of all my lonely feelings
from being left behind so much lately.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.130
Use that rod of yours to reduce every last one to dust!

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:54.880
You were lonely, Ancestor?

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.750
<b>DYNASTY WARRIORS: SHAMIKO</b>

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:56.580
Okay, time to start!

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:57.880
Go get 'em, Sis!

00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:58.210
<b>DYNASTY WARRIORS: SHAMIKO</b>

00:18:56.750 --> 00:18:58.210
<b>Go get 'em!</b>

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:00.290
Bring it ooooon!

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:00.540
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:03.130
Take this! And that! There's still so many of them!

00:19:01.170 --> 00:19:01.460
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:02.460
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:03.500
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:09.210
Hiyah! Hooyah! Oorah!

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:04.460
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:05.500
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:06.500
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.630
Keep it up, you've got 29,950 more to go!

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:07.580
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:08.540
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:09.500
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:13.130
That's a ridiculous amount! All of this
just because you were feeling lonely?!

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:15.250
Well, I really can't stand being by myself.

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:18.580
If you don't finish them all off, then you'll have
to take me to the amusement park, kay?

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:21.540
That's not a problem, you should just ask
and I'll take you any time!

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:25.170
By the way, I graciously added a counter
of how many you've defeated on the bottom right.

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:26.790
What "bottom right"?!

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:33.960
<b>DEFEATED</b>

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:38.790
Hiyah! Hooyah! Booyah! Fooyah!

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:27.420
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:28.460
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:29.460
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.460
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:31.670
You gotta go faster.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:31.460
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:33.960
Your body will end up waking up at this rate!

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:32.460
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:33.460
<b>POOF</b>

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.540
Hey, Ryo. Give her some advice would you?

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:38.790
Shamiko doesn't really understand how weapons work.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:40.880
Hey, Big Sis?

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.460
Swinging your weapon around
like that will tire you out quickly.

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:47.250
I think you should try turning it into something from
a fairy tale, since we're in the dreamscape right now.

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:50.000
Use your imagination to create something powerful,

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:52.920
like "a sword that can disintegrate
a whole continent when its unsheathed."

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:54.380
Disintegrate a continent...?

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:57.130
CONTINENT SWOOOOORD!

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:59.580
Oh phooey! I only made a sword
that looks like it was scribbled on!

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:05.380
<b>CONTINENT</b>

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:05.380
<b>SWORD</b>

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:05.380
<b>DEFEATED</b>

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:01.880
I'm sorry, Ryo! I'm just not imaginative enough!

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:05.380
I can't even picture what
disintegrating a continent would be like!

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:09.580
Okay, then why don't you try taking a reference
from one of those old video games you like?

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:11.170
Maybe a magic staff or something?

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:13.040
Oh! I think I can manage that.

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:19.000
<b>Demon in thought</b>

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:18.790
Yeah, that might work. Like that one staff...
or even that one would be good!

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.130
FLAME STAFF!

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:24.580
<b>DEFEATED</b>

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:26.380
STORM STAFF!

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:30.540
<b>DEFEATED</b>

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:32.960
Time for a little break! Come on, Snack Staff!

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.290
Is that really necessary?

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:36.000
<b>ZAP</b>

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:36.000
<b>ZAP</b>

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:36.380
<b>ZAP</b>

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:36.710
<b>ZAP</b>

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:36.710
<b>ZAP</b>

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:37.040
<b>ZAP</b>

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:37.040
<b>ZAP</b>

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:37.500
<b>ZAP</b>

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:44.290
<b>DEFEATED</b>

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:38.670
I don't know why,

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:41.130
but the Snack Staff defeated a whole bunch of them!

00:20:41.250 --> 00:20:44.290
I guess the real cure to loneliness is eating tasty sweets.

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:45.420
Last one!

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:46.790
GLACIAL STAFF!

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:51.460
<b>DEFEATED</b>

00:20:47.630 --> 00:20:50.040
I'm impressed. I didn't think you'd actually get them all!

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.500
I'm finally getting the hang of this!

00:20:51.630 --> 00:20:53.500
And you have Ryo's advice to thank for that.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:55.830
Good job! I'm glad we got to goof around together, Ryo!

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:58.500
To be honest, meeting you in person
was the best thing about today!

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:00.880
You're another one of my cute descendants.

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:04.380
I hope you'll work hard alongside your sister
to ensure that our clan has a bright future!

00:21:04.670 --> 00:21:05.250
Okay!

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:08.580
Do you think I could take a picture of you, Ancestor?

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:13.500
Hmmm. I don't think cameras inside the dreamscape
would respond with those on the outside.

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:15.790
Wait. Actually, that gives me an idea.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.000
Meanwhile, over at Banda Terrace...

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:22.540
This homework is killing me. I can't stay awake, snore...

00:21:21.080 --> 00:21:23.920
1303... 1304...

00:21:26.000 --> 00:21:29.380
Are you awake, my descendants?
I need you to put a camera in front of me!

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:31.080
<b>CLENCH</b>

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:31.960
Hocus focus!

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:32.500
<b>CLICK</b>

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:34.420
What did you just do?

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:35.750
Heh heh heh, triple heh.

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.540
<b>HEH</b>

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.540
<b>HEH</b>

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.540
<b>HEH</b>

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.540
<b>TRIPLE</b>

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.540
<b>HEH</b>

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:36.420
Thoughtography!

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:37.420
What's that?

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:40.040
I've been secretly practicing it ever since
my seal started to come undone.

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:44.330
I just sent a visualization of what can be seen
in my sealed space to that camera.

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:49.130
It should be a majestic pic of me! Now you can print a
huge copy out, frame it, and hang it for all to see!

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:52.960
I get the feeling that's going to leave
the wrong impression. Let me go and fetch Momo, first.

00:21:54.380 --> 00:21:55.880
15,000...

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:57.210
Momo!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:58.880
Welcome back. How'd it go?

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:01.960
The practice really helped me to improve!
And I made some good memories, too!

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:04.710
You used thoughtography to capture
a picture of Ms. Lilith's true form?

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:06.880
Now you can use that as reference
to create my next doll vessel!

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:08.710
Ah, there's data in the camera!

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:13.750
That's a haunted photograph.

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:15.920
Guess I need more practice.

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:20.250
Don't give up, Lilith! Glamorize and accessorize until you
become a demon who looks fantastic in a photograph!

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:21.630
No, don't bother with that. Practice isn't what you need.

00:22:21.830 --> 00:22:23.750
You were so close, Ancestor!

00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:25.790
Snore, snore, mikan.

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:46.670
We met again. It's drama?

00:22:46.670 --> 00:22:49.670
I'll go tell someone at once

00:22:49.790 --> 00:22:52.540
As soon as possible

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:55.170
Oh, even the post box says "Good morning"

00:22:55.170 --> 00:22:57.380
Even my tail is sharp

00:22:57.380 --> 00:23:01.170
If our usual members gather and jump over the white lines

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:03.920
Today will start, too

00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:07.710
A sudden mystery

00:23:07.830 --> 00:23:11.080
Makes me feel dizzy and at a loss

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:15.630
But we will hold hands and go anywhere we want

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:22.630
The city is turning and shining

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.540
Around and around many times

00:23:25.540 --> 00:23:28.250
The night mixed with dreams

00:23:28.250 --> 00:23:31.080
Will make you blossom

00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:34.080
The tetragon that surrounds four sides

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:36.960
Ah, a bouquet for our neighborhood

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:39.920
Hey, now, just a little bit more

00:23:40.170 --> 00:23:43.920
Show me the flowers secretly

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:47.580
Once more if I get greedy!

00:23:56.040 --> 00:24:10.960
<b>PREVIEW</b>

00:23:56.710 --> 00:23:59.420
It feels like I trained a lot of skills over summer vacation!

00:23:59.420 --> 00:24:00.960
Now it's time for the new semester to start.

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:03.250
I finally get to wear the same uniform as you and Momo!

00:24:03.250 --> 00:24:04.630
But I'm worried that I might not fit in,

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:05.960
since I'm a transfer student.

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:07.920
There's nothing to worry about, you'll be fine.

00:24:06.830 --> 00:24:10.960
<b>NEW SEMESTER! THE MAGICAL GIRL'S NEW DUTY!</b>

00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:10.000
All right, I have to attend to my committee duties.

00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:10.670
See you later.
